  "core_thesis": "BWXT is a structurally irreplaceable defense-nuclear franchise — the sole-source supplier of U.S. naval nuclear components for over a century — whose $7.26B backlog (49% expansion in nine months) provides multi-year revenue visibility that consensus underweights. The market is currently discounting the stock for near-term margin compression and leverage accumulation, but we believe these are transitory execution headwinds accompanying a deliberate capacity expansion cycle, not structural deterioration. As contract mix normalizes and backlog converts, FCF generation will accelerate toward debt service requirements, re-rating the stock from a risk-discount to a quality-premium multiple. The variant bet is that the 2028-2030 refinancing wall is manageable given contracted revenue coverage, while the bear case on DOGE-driven defense cuts structurally exempts naval nuclear propulsion.",
