}","__type__":"PhaseOutput","structured":{"bear_case":[{"title":"Margin compression may be structural, not cyclical","evidence":"As shown in Business Quality and Financial Health: operating margins deteriorated from ~15% to 8-10% and gross margins compressed from 24-25% to 21-22% over the most recent two quarters — if this reflects permanent contract repricing or cost escalation rather than mix shift, FCF recovery assumptions underpinning the bull case are invalid."},{"title":"$1.25B 2030 debt maturity dwarfs current FCF capacity","evidence":"As shown in Financial Health and Risk Assessment: the $1.25B single-tranche 2030 maturity represents ~4x trailing annualized FCF of ~$300M; at a D/E of 1.63x with declining FCF conversion (6-7% of revenue), the refinancing wall leaves limited margin for error if interest rates remain elevated or revenue growth decelerates."},{"title":"68% government revenue dependency under fiscal scrutiny","evidence":"As shown in Risk Assessment: U.S. Government contracts constitute 68% of consolidated revenues under DOE and defense appropriations cycles that face DOGE-era fiscal scrutiny — even a modest appropriations delay or contract scope reduction could materially disrupt near-term FCF and backlog conversion timing."},{"title":"Stock has already run ahead of analyst price targets","evidence":"As shown in Sentiment & Narrative and Technical & Market Structure: analyst consensus average price target of $210 implies ~5.7% downside from $222.77; a Seaport Global downgrade to Neutral in January 2026 signals institutional recognition that risk/reward has deteriorated at current levels, capping near-term multiple expansion."},{"title":"Sudden 65% debt increase raises capital allocation questions","evidence":"As flagged in Quick Screen and confirmed in Financial Health: the sharp leverage increase to D/E 1.63x combined with margin compression creates an unfavorable simultaneous deterioration in both earnings quality and balance sheet safety — the