s $110-150M+ in annual interest expense — yet reported interest expense is only $0.01B, suggesting either the debt was raised very recently or is structured as convertible/zero-coupon. This ambiguity makes DSCR analysis impossible and refinancing risk unquantifiable, which is itself a material negative for institutional credit assessment.\n\nThe capital allocation rationale hinges on whether the AI data center buildout can generate ROIC sufficient to service $3.69B in debt. Analyst revenue estimates imply $3.52B by mid-2029 from current TTM revenue of approximately $0.7B — a 5x growth assumption [Source: FMP /analyst-estimates]. Even at 20% EBITDA margins (generous for a co-location/mining hybrid), this implies $700M EBITDA against a debt load that was $3.69B in Q2 2025 and growing with CapEx. The leverage ratio implied by these numbers is not self-sustaining without continued equity or debt issuance, confirming the capital structure is episodically rather than organically funded.\n\nInsider disposition is unambiguous: both Co-CEOs sold a combined $72.8M in September 2025 with zero buying [Source: FMP /insider-trading], removing any management alignment argument. The JP Morgan Underweight is the only sell-side signal that aligns with this concern [Source: FMP /analyst-ratings]. The current ratio of 4.96x provides near-term liquidity comfort, but this is a snapshot of freshly-raised capital rather than evidence of sustainable cash generation. Financial health score of 38 reflects serious structural leverage concerns offset only by the large cash buffer and currently adequate current ratio.",
