}","__type__":"CategoryResult","category":"Growth & Earnings","structured":{"score":52,"analysis":"IREN Limited presents one of the most complex earnings profiles in the crypto-adjacent infrastructure space: a business that is simultaneously a Bitcoin miner (exposed to volatile BTC prices and halving economics), a data center operator, and an emerging AI/HPC infrastructure provider. Disentangling these dynamics is essential to any growth and earnings assessment.

The historical revenue trajectory is undeniably impressive in magnitude. From $0.05B in Q1 FY2025 to $0.24B in Q1 FY2026 — a 341.8% increase — IREN has clearly expanded its compute capacity and benefited from Bitcoin price appreciation [Source: FMP /income-statement quarterly]. However, the Q2 FY2026 data is jarring: revenue fell back to $0.12B (+2.8% YoY) while gross margins collapsed to 10.7% and net margins hit -84.1% (-$0.52 EPS). This is almost certainly a reflection of Bitcoin mining economics deteriorating post-halving combined with fixed infrastructure costs, but it illustrates the earnings fragility inherent in the model.

