Forward analyst estimates project revenue scaling from approximately $0.5-0.6B run-rate today to $3.52B by June 2029 — a roughly 6x increase over three to four years [Source: FMP /analyst-estimates]. This growth is likely predicated on AI/HPC data center ramp-up and continued Bitcoin price support. However, forward EPS estimates are universally $0.00, suggesting analysts expect capital intensity, depreciation, and interest expense from the recent debt raise (LT debt jumped from $0.96B to $3.69B in Q2 FY2026, D/E rising to 1.53x) to absorb all earnings for the foreseeable future [Source: FMP /balance-sheet quarterly].

CapEx intensity is extreme — $0.28-0.44B per quarter in recent periods — funded by a large balance sheet ($3.26B cash in Q2 FY2026) built through what appears to be equity and debt issuance [Source: FMP /cash-flow-statement quarterly]. FCF is correspondingly erratic: +$0.35B in Q2 FY2026 (likely including Bitcoin asset monetization) versus -$0.49B in Q3 FY2025. The DCF model produces a deeply negative intrinsic value, reflecting terminal value sensitivity to discount rate assumptions given the capital-intensive, low-EBITDA present state.

