nalysts collectively do not expect Rocket Lab to achieve GAAP profitability in the next three-plus years. The implied revenue CAGR from current levels to 2028 estimates is roughly 25-30%, a deceleration from current rates. This is likely conservative if Neutron launches successfully, but Neutron remains a significant execution risk that is unresolved.\n\nThe DCF intrinsic value calculation is negative (-$59.35), which is a mechanical artifact of negative cash flows projected forward — it underscores that at current burn rates, terminal value assumptions carry almost the entire weight of any bullish thesis. The 40.2B market cap is pricing in a dramatically different future than the present financial profile suggests. For growth-oriented investors, the gross margin trajectory warrants watching closely as the most meaningful leading indicator of eventual earnings power. For earnings-focused investors, there is little here to anchor on for at least 2-3 years.",
