  "core_thesis": "Rocket Lab (RKLB) is a competitively differentiated small-launch and space systems platform with genuine operational momentum—gross margins expanding from 26% to 38% over eight quarters and revenue accelerating to 48% YoY growth—but the $40.2B market capitalization is almost entirely a bet on Neutron medium-lift rocket success, a single-point-of-failure with no near-term revenue contribution. As shown in Valuation, the DCF intrinsic value is mathematically negative at -$59.35/share, and as shown in Risk Assessment, the base Electron + Space Systems franchise cannot support the current multiple even under generous assumptions. At a 67x trailing revenue multiple with no path to positive FCF through 2028, the risk/reward is structurally unfavorable for new long positions despite the quality of the underlying technology narrative.",
